/** # Command Line Reference
To compile and execute a script file, the cmpl application must be invoked with the corresponding arguments.

>cmpl \[global options\]... \[file \[file options\]...\]...
*/
inline "*usage";

/* note:
All the text of the documentation is in the doc comments of the inlined files,
only the placeholders are replaced with generated text by `-dump.md`:
- `inline "*example:tail";`: the rest of the file as example.
- `inline "*example:<n>";`: the next n lines of the file as example.
- `inline "*library";`, `inline "*library:<unit>";`: the documented library symbols.
- `inline "*opcode:<name>";`: the generated properties of an instruction.
- `inline "*usage";`: the command line options and examples.
*/
